course: dictionary
lesson: 8719
title: A word that stands guard
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A sentinel is a guard or watcher. «One meerkat stands guard as a sentinel, watching for eagles and jackals» tells you the meerkat's job: it keeps watch so the group can see danger coming.
explain: The word can also describe a thing that stands like a guard. «A tree standing sentinel on a hill» means the tree stands still and watches over the hill, the way a guard would. Ask yourself: what is doing the watching, and what is it watching for?
explain: Sentinel can also mean something that gives early warning. Scientists use sentinel animals or plants to warn of pollution, a bit like canaries in coal mines. The word always points to something that keeps watch.
fact: A sentinel is a guard or watcher.
fact: «Stand sentinel» means stand still and watch.
fact: In history and stories, sentinels guard castle walls and gates.
fact: In science, a sentinel species is an animal or plant that gives early warning of pollution.
fact: Sentinel is a noun. You can have one sentinel or many sentinels.
exercise: «One meerkat stands guard as a sentinel, watching for eagles and jackals.» What is the meerkat's job here? | *To keep watch for danger | To sleep in the sun | To sing to the group | To dig for food all day
exercise: «A tree standing sentinel on a hill» What is the tree doing? | Falling over in the wind | Growing fruit for the birds | Moving quickly down the hill | *Standing still and watching over the hill
exercise: Scientists use sentinel animals to warn of pollution. Why are they called sentinels? | They are very tall | They are made of stone | *They give early warning, like a guard | They are always the fastest runners
test: What does «stand sentinel» mean? | To sit down and sleep | *To stand still and watch | To run away quickly | To dance in a circle
test: A sentry is another word for a sentinel. What does a sentry do? | Tells jokes to the children | *Stands guard and watches for danger | Sells tickets at the gate | Bakes bread for the castle
exam: In «a lone sentinel on the hill», what does sentinel mean? | A soft blanket for the cold | A type of bird that sings at dawn | A school bell that rings at break | *Something that stands like a guard and watches over a place
